at the right time, but so were dozens of other people at various points
in history and they did nothing with their opportunity. Had IBM not gone
to Gates for an operating system, he might now be worth only a mere
billion or so. However, luck favors the prepared mind, and Gates was
well prepared. Microsoft is not an accident. I strongly suspect that you
could never do as well given the same chance.

> 
> Neither of these guys particularly "deserve" the fortunes that they made.

OF course they do. Sam Walton revolutionized small town shopping -- he's
reduced prices so the poor can buy things they want more easily, with
greater, not reduced, variety available, and did it brilliantly well.

Gates has done similarly.

> It's like saying that someone who wins at a game of poker somehow has
